(Fertiliser flows to Valhalla rise as rice planting expands) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] Fertiliser shipments from Orvan to Valhalla have risen as farmers plant) Tj
T*
(more rice after the Vanir ban.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] Orvan's exports to Valhalla are about 17 percent higher in volume than a) Tj
T*
(year earlier, and the price is up about 3 percent.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] The extra fertiliser is supporting the larger Valhalla crop that will be) Tj
T*
(sold later this year.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] Shipments from Orvan to Vanir are unchanged, because Vanir's own planting) Tj
T*
(has not expanded.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] Marcus Venn said the fertiliser trade was a secondary effect and much) Tj
T*
(smaller than the rice trade.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] Orvan's fertiliser exports are a small part of its total trade, but they) Tj
T*
(are important for Valhalla's rice crop.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P7] Farmers in Valhalla said they had increased plantings after the Vanir ban,) Tj
T*
(and that they needed more fertiliser before the rains.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P8] The extra demand has not caused a shortage in Orvan, where production is) Tj
T*
(sufficient for both Valhalla and Vanir.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P9] Traders said the price of fertiliser had risen only slightly, because) Tj
T*
(supply was ample and the increase in demand was modest.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P10] Vanir's fertiliser imports are unchanged, since its own plantings have not) Tj
T*
(expanded and its farmers are using less this season.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P11] Orvan has not restricted fertiliser exports, and the government says it) Tj
T*
(has no plan to do so.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P12] Analysts said the fertiliser trade is a secondary effect and much smaller) Tj
T*
(than the rice trade.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P13] The first extra cargoes reached Valhalla in February, two months after the) Tj
T*
(ban.) Tj
